<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  RUT_FoundryFloor_MeltChannels.xml      UtinniPatches · FORGE_MECHANICS_1 F4
  ============================================================================
  forge_kit_spec.md F4: "melt channels (impassable)... heat as the wall."
  Uses RM_GenStep_TerrainChannels (new this pass,
  src/RimMandrake/EnvironmentalHazards/Source/ — see that class's own header)
  to paint vanilla LavaDeep — CONFIRMED via RimSage this pass:
  ParentName="LavaBase", passability Impassable, dangerous true, native
  burnDamage/burnIntervalTicks/ignitePawnsIntervalTicks fields (read by the
  stock Verse/HediffGiver_Terrain.cs every tick, no C# of this mod's own
  involved) — exactly the "open melt as the wall" framing this same item's
  own spike pass already resolved (FORGE_MECHANICS_1.md spike finding 1:
  "any walkable melt/scald surface in the tower floors should crib
  LavaShallow's own field values... No C# needed for either behaviour").
  LavaDeep, not LavaShallow, chosen specifically because it is Impassable:
  GenStep_Scatterer's own `spotMustBeStandable` field (Verse/
  GenStep_Scatterer.cs, read this pass) rejects any cell that fails
  IntVec3.Standable, and Impassable terrain always fails that check — so
  painting LavaDeep here is what makes the hard-ban-#1 guard on
  RUT_FoundryFloor_SalvageCache.xml / RUT_FoundryFloor_TenderSpawn.xml
  actually effective, not merely decorative. No existing lava/melt
  TerrainDef found anywhere in this repo's own RUT_/RM_ content (checked
  this pass) — LavaDeep is a vanilla Odyssey def already searched for and
  confirmed present (RimSage), so nothing new was invented here.

  order 300 — after Terrain (210, vanilla, base ground already painted) and
  before ScatterRuinsSimple (750, vanilla) and this floor's own two
  set-piece scatterers (850/860), so every later genStep's own site search
  already sees the melt on the terrain grid.

  Tuning (channel count/length/width, turn chance) is entirely this pass's
  own INVENTED choice — the spec names no channel geometry, only "open
  melt... heat as the wall." A live/quicktest pass is owed to judge the
  actual density/legibility of the result (no bridge access this task).
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <GenStepDef MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">
    <defName>RUT_FoundryFloor_MeltChannels</defName>
    <order>300</order>
    <genStep Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_GenStep_TerrainChannels">
      <terrainDef>LavaDeep</terrainDef>
      <channelCountRange>3~5</channelCountRange>
      <channelLengthRange>30~55</channelLengthRange>
      <channelWidthRange>1~2</channelWidthRange>
      <turnChancePerStep>0.35</turnChancePerStep>
    </genStep>
  </GenStepDef>

</Defs>
